==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|loudly}}, equivalent to {{af|en|loud|-ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|loud′lē}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈlaʊdli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-loudly.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|loud|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[loud]] manner; at a [[high]] [[volume]].
#: {{syn|en|loud}}
#: {{antonyms|en|quietly}}
#: {{ux|en|He spoke '''loudly''' so that his brother could hear him from across the street.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=R[obert] S[tephen] Hawker|authorlink=Robert Stephen Hawker|chapter=The Wreck|title=Echoes from Old Cornwall|location=London|publisher=Joseph Masters,{{nb...|Aldersgate Street.}}|year=1846|section=stanza X|page=76|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=KbFG_INx-DIC&pg=PA76|oclc=3365560|passage=And still when '''loudliest''' howls the storm, / And darkliest [[lour|lowers]] his native sky, / The king's fierce soul is in that form, / The warrior's spirit threatens nigh!}}

